        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "0.5 mol"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "Mr of H₂O = (2 × 1) + 16 = 18, so the molar mass is 18 g/mol. Using n = m/M = 36/18 = 2 mol."
